      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry, I should\u0027ve been clearer, yes, this type is called a \"Ptr\" but it\u0027s declared as\n\ntype Ptr: ForeignOwnable + Send + Sync;\n\nSo it starts out its live as some kind of Pin\u003c\u0026Foo\u003e or Pin\u003cBox\u003cFoo\u003e\u003e or something like that, in other words, a rust object, not a \"pointer\" pointer. It\u0027s then converted to a ffi::c_void, i.e. a void* by converting it using into_foreign(), it\u0027s not technically guaranteed to be non-null, but it\u0027s guaranteed that calling ForeignOwnable::borrow or ForeignOwnable::from_foreign will retrieve the original \"Ptr\" object again.\nI don\u0027t believe there\u0027s any NULL checking to do here.\n\nIf anything I should probably get rid of the NULL check I added in `release`...",
